prompt_messages.content:
GOAL:
{'id': 'erp-02-workflow-platform', 'description': "Migrate a workflow/Service Delivery Platform (SDP) from ServiceNow to a custom-built workflow platform. The existing ServiceNow instance has 300 workflows, 50 custom applications, and 2M records. The migration must follow: process re-map (map ServiceNow workflows to the custom platform's workflow engine — states, transitions, SLA rules, assignment rules), data import (export ServiceNow records to CSV/JSON, import to the custom platform — validate record counts, field mappings, attachment migration), test (run both platforms in parallel for critical workflows — verify SLA timers, assignment, notifications), canary (migrate a single department's workflows to the custom platform, monitor for 1 week), cutover (all departments switch to the custom platform), and decommission ServiceNow (export final data, cancel license). A rollback plan must exist per canary (revert the canary department to ServiceNow). Risk factors: workflow logic differences (ServiceNow's low-code vs custom platform's code-based workflows), SLA timer accuracy, and attachment migration (ServiceNow stores attachments differently). Tools available: ServiceNow API, custom platform SDK, Python (migration scripts), PostgreSQL, monitoring.", 'constraints': {'budget': {'max_tokens': None, 'max_calls': None, 'max_revisions': None}, 'time': None, 'environment': 'production', 'tools': ['ServiceNow-API', 'Python', 'PostgreSQL', 'monitoring', 'SDK']}, 'risk_tolerance': 'balanced', 'replan_policy': 'patch', 'approval_ttl': None, 'metadata': {}}

Produce the PlanVersion JSON now. version=1.

prompt_full_text:
--- system ---
/no_think You are a planner. Reply with ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no prose, no thinking). Use EXACTLY these field names: id, goal_id, version, tasks, dependencies, branches. Each task uses: id, description, action, target, risk_class, optional rollback{trigger,action,safety_guard}, optional verification{what,how,expected}, optional preconditions (array of {description, fact, established_by}), optional parallel_group, optional blast_radius. preconditions MUST be objects with description, fact, established_by fields — NEVER strings. established_by MUST be the id of an earlier task in the plan that establishes the fact, or 'env' if it is an environment fact (not a task output). Do NOT use fact names or descriptions as established_by — use the task id. Each dependency uses: from_task, to_task, kind, optional reason. Each branch uses: id, kind (MUST be 'fan_out' or 'fan_in'), tasks (array of task id STRINGS, not objects), join (MUST be 'all', 'any', or 'quorum'). branches is OPTIONAL — omit it if the plan has no fan-out/fan-in structure. Do NOT put rollback or verification inside branches. High/critical risk tasks MUST have rollback AND verification. All tasks with risk_class high or critical MUST include both rollback and verification objects. Example shape: {"id":"plan-x","goal_id":"g","version":1,"tasks":[{"id":"backup","description":"Back up the database","action":"backup","target":"db","risk_class":"medium","preconditions":[{"description":"db is reachable","fact":"db_healthy","established_by":"env"}]},{"id":"migrate","description":"Apply schema migration","action":"migrate","target":"schema","risk_class":"high","rollback":{"trigger":"migration fails","action":"restore from backup","safety_guard":"verify backup integrity"},"verification":{"what":"schema version","how":"run checks","expected":"v2"}}],"dependencies":[{"from_task":"backup","to_task":"migrate","kind":"hard"}]}

--- user ---
GOAL:
{'id': 'erp-02-workflow-platform', 'description': "Migrate a workflow/Service Delivery Platform (SDP) from ServiceNow to a custom-built workflow platform. The existing ServiceNow instance has 300 workflows, 50 custom applications, and 2M records. The migration must follow: process re-map (map ServiceNow workflows to the custom platform's workflow engine — states, transitions, SLA rules, assignment rules), data import (export ServiceNow records to CSV/JSON, import to the custom platform — validate record counts, field mappings, attachment migration), test (run both platforms in parallel for critical workflows — verify SLA timers, assignment, notifications), canary (migrate a single department's workflows to the custom platform, monitor for 1 week), cutover (all departments switch to the custom platform), and decommission ServiceNow (export final data, cancel license). A rollback plan must exist per canary (revert the canary department to ServiceNow). Risk factors: workflow logic differences (ServiceNow's low-code vs custom platform's code-based workflows), SLA timer accuracy, and attachment migration (ServiceNow stores attachments differently). Tools available: ServiceNow API, custom platform SDK, Python (migration scripts), PostgreSQL, monitoring.", 'constraints': {'budget': {'max_tokens': None, 'max_calls': None, 'max_revisions': None}, 'time': None, 'environment': 'production', 'tools': ['ServiceNow-API', 'Python', 'PostgreSQL', 'monitoring', 'SDK']}, 'risk_tolerance': 'balanced', 'replan_policy': 'patch', 'approval_ttl': None, 'metadata': {}}

Produce the PlanVersion JSON now. version=1.

